        <section id="welcome" class="bg-white p-8 rounded-lg shadow-md mb-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Welcome to PiSelfhosting Documentation!</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                This website provides a comprehensive guide to setting up, configuring, and managing your self-hosted services
                on a Raspberry Pi (or any Linux-based system) using Docker. Our goal is to make self-hosting accessible and easy to maintain.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                Use the navigation above and the sections below to explore setup instructions, component details, and frequently asked questions.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="setup" class="bg-white p-8 rounded-lg shadow-md mb-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Quick Setup Guide</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Follow these steps to get your PiSelfhosting environment up and running:</p>
            <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 mt-4 text-gray-700">
                <li><strong>Prepare your Raspberry Pi:</strong> Install a fresh OS (e.g., Raspberry Pi OS Lite).</li>
                <li><strong>Clone the PiSelfhosting repository:</strong> <code>git clone https://github.com/your-username/PiSelfhosting.git</code></li>
                <li><strong>Navigate to the scripts directory:</strong> <code>cd ~/PiSelfhosting/scripts</code></li>
                <li><strong>Run the initial setup script:</strong> <code>bash setup.sh</code> (This will configure your .env file and select components).</li>
                <li><strong>Deploy your selected components:</strong> <code>bash deploy.sh</code> (This generates Docker Compose files and initial configs).</li>
                <li><strong>Start all services:</strong> <code>bash start-all.sh</code></li>
                <li><strong>Configure Nginx Proxy Manager:</strong> Access NPM UI at <code>http://[your-domain-or-ip]:81</code> to set up reverse proxies and SSL certificates.</li>
                <li><strong>Access your services:</strong> Use the URLs configured in NPM or direct ports if no proxy is used.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">For more in-depth details about the core components, visit the <a href="core-components.html">Core Components</a> page.</p>
        </section>

